# D-NETMESH-UMOUNT-RELEASES-TO-DEPARTED-PEER-200MS-EACH: same-build A/B of
# dl_relall_skip_unreachable (1 = a release-all sends nothing more to a master
# a release could not reach; 0 = the same-build control, every grant retried
# 3 x 100 ms).  tests/mpath/umount_pair_race.sh makes the race certain: B (the
# group's last node) steps its release-all dl_relall_step_ms per release so it
# outlasts A's whole unmount, which starts PF_GAP_S later.  The row leaves both
# nodes unmounted, so every row is preceded by a prep.
# Control must show failed sends to A (FAILED_SENDS > 0) and a long B unmount;
# the fix must show P-RELALL-MASTER-UNREACHABLE and B's unmount inside its
# bound.  A control with no failed send means the harness did not reach the
# race and the pair proves nothing.
# Bounds: prep_cluster 300 (tests/suite/manifest); the row's own --budget 300
# (its header: gate + warm-up 20 s + load 30 s + stop/verify 15 s + stepped
# release-all ~20 s + slack 30 s + readback 10 s = ~150 s) + 30 s for
# lap_chain's marker read and result write = 330.
# Knobs go in as PF_KNOBS: lap_queue.sh treats any '=' after the script name
# as an assignment.
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 4/net/mesh/mpath --group g4 prep_cluster
330 PF_KNOBS='dl_relall_skip_unreachable=0' tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh row 4/net/mesh/mpath g4 uprc1 tests/mpath/umount_pair_race.sh --budget 300
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 4/net/mesh/mpath --group g4 prep_cluster
330 PF_KNOBS='dl_relall_skip_unreachable=1' tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh row 4/net/mesh/mpath g4 uprf1 tests/mpath/umount_pair_race.sh --budget 300
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 4/net/mesh/mpath --group g4 prep_cluster
330 PF_KNOBS='dl_relall_skip_unreachable=0' tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh row 4/net/mesh/mpath g4 uprc2 tests/mpath/umount_pair_race.sh --budget 300
300 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 4/net/mesh/mpath --group g4 prep_cluster
330 PF_KNOBS='dl_relall_skip_unreachable=1' tests/mpath/lap_chain.sh row 4/net/mesh/mpath g4 uprf2 tests/mpath/umount_pair_race.sh --budget 300
